CVE-2026-21728 exp:2026-08-13

# GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw: kin-openapi ValidationHandler.Load() silently substitutes
# a no-op auth function when none is configured, letting requests bypass any
# security requirement declared in an OpenAPI spec (CVSS 9.1).
# Why no fix: Affects grafana:13.0.4-ubuntu — re-verified 2026-08-03, including
# checking the newer 13.1.1-ubuntu tag directly (still vendors kin-openapi
# v0.140.0, below the fixed 0.144.0, and introduces a larger set of other HIGH
# CVEs — not worth switching to for this alone); fix ships in 0.144.0 but no
# Grafana release has picked it up yet.
# Why not exploitable: exploitation requires an application to run kin-openapi's
# ValidationHandler as HTTP middleware over an endpoint with no AuthenticationFunc
# configured. Grafana's own dashboard/API auth (session cookie / API key / OAuth)
# gates requests ahead of any such internal validation layer, and in our
# deployment Grafana is reachable only by authenticated administrators on an
# internal/loopback network, never directly by untrusted external clients — same
# exposure posture as every other Grafana finding in this file.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw exp:2026-08-10

# CVE-2026-33811: net package DoS in Go stdlib.
